  "question": {
    "text": "There is some change in length when a <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>33000</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi></math> tensile force is applied on a steel rod of the area of cross-section<math><msup><mrow><mn>10</mn></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>&nbsp;</mi></mrow></msup><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></math>. The change of temperature required to produce the same elongation, if the steel rod is heated, is (The modulus of elasticity is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn><mo>×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>11</mn></msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi><mo>&nbsp;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></math> and the coefficient of linear expansion of steel is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>.1</mo><mo>×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&nbsp;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">℃</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>)"
  },
